---
import data from '../data/ecg-library.json';
const s = (data as any).source;
---
<aside class="mt-10 p-5 rounded-lg border border-clinical-200 dark:border-clinical-700 bg-clinical-50 dark:bg-clinical-800/40">
  <h2 class="font-heading text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-clinical-500 dark:text-clinical-400 mb-2">
    Source and licence
  </h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-clinical-600 dark:text-clinical-400">
    Every tracing here is rendered from raw signal in
    <a href={s.url} class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">{s.name} v{s.version}</a>,
    an open dataset of clinical 12-lead ECGs, and is used under
    <a href={s.licenseUrl} class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">{s.license}</a>.
    Diagnostic labels are the dataset's cardiologist-assigned SCP-ECG statements, not my own reading
    and not a machine's.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-clinical-500 dark:text-clinical-400">{s.citation}</p>
  <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-clinical-500 dark:text-clinical-400">{s.paper}</p>
  <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-clinical-500 dark:text-clinical-400">{s.physionet}</p>
</aside>
